%% Canonical Async-Operation Runtime Spine (Quiz, State-recommendation)
%% Descriptive. Specializes system 05-runtime/ai-quiz + state-pipeline; ADR-006 / ADR-011.
%% NOTE: the operation-record <-> trusted-context relationship is behavioral, not a storage prescription.
%% No queue/job technology is implied. Study Assistant interaction model is Open/Deferred (not shown).

sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant Web as Web / API process
    participant Store as Persistence (Open)
    participant Worker as Worker process
    participant LAI as Learning & AI capability
    participant LLM as Madar-owned LLM interface

    Client->>Web: submit operation
    Web->>Web: authn / authz / server-derived context
    Web->>Web: enforce idempotency boundary (ADR-011)
    Web->>Store: persist operation (initial state) + establish trusted operation context
    Web-->>Client: acknowledge (operation id)

    Note over Worker: reconstruct trusted context from server-created state\n(never client-derived / unscoped-privileged)
    Worker->>Store: transition -> Processing
    Worker->>LAI: invoke capability (trusted context + bounded source input)
    LAI->>LLM: (may cross the LLM seam)
    LLM-->>LAI: model output
    LAI-->>Worker: result | failure

    alt success
        Worker->>Store: persist result + terminal Succeeded
    else failure / timeout
        Worker->>Store: persist failure + terminal Failed (no partial result)
    end

    Client->>Web: poll status/result (where the contract exposes polling)
    Web-->>Client: terminal state / result
